WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.469
- [Voiceover] So we have
g of x being defined

00:02.469 --> 00:06.636
as the log of 3x when zero is
less than x is less than three

00:08.163 --> 00:11.389
and four minus x times the log of nine

00:11.389 --> 00:15.056
when x is greater than or equal to three.

00:16.555 --> 00:19.421
So based on this definition of g of x,

00:19.421 --> 00:21.279
we want to find the limit of g of x

00:21.279 --> 00:24.415
as x approaches three, and once again,

00:24.415 --> 00:27.735
this three is right at
the interface between

00:27.735 --> 00:30.722
these two clauses or these two cases.

00:30.722 --> 00:34.709
We go to this first case when
x is between zero and three,

00:34.709 --> 00:37.359
when it's greater than
zero and less than three,

00:37.359 --> 00:39.908
and then at three, we hit this case.

00:39.908 --> 00:42.318
So in order to find the
limit, we want to find

00:42.318 --> 00:44.315
the limit from the left hand side

00:44.315 --> 00:46.303
which will have us dealing
with this situation

00:46.303 --> 00:49.282
'cause if we're less than
three we're in this clause,

00:49.282 --> 00:51.897
and we also want to find a
limit from the right hand side

00:51.897 --> 00:54.911
which would put us in this
clause right over here,

00:54.911 --> 00:57.179
and then if both of those limits exist

00:57.179 --> 00:59.891
and if they are the same,
then that is going to be

00:59.891 --> 01:02.560
the limit of this, so let's do that.

01:02.560 --> 01:05.957
So let me first go from
the left hand side.

01:05.957 --> 01:09.615
So the limit as x
approaches three from values

01:09.615 --> 01:12.572
less than three, so we're
gonna approach from the left

01:12.572 --> 01:16.322
of g of x, well, this
is equivalent to saying

01:18.564 --> 01:22.758
this is the limit as x approaches three

01:22.758 --> 01:24.444
from the negative side.

01:24.444 --> 01:27.936
When x is less than three,
which is what's happening here,

01:27.936 --> 01:29.946
we're approaching three from the left,

01:29.946 --> 01:32.022
we're in this clause right over here.

01:32.022 --> 01:33.889
So we're gonna be
operating right over there.

01:33.889 --> 01:37.568
That is what g of x is when
we are less than three.

01:37.568 --> 01:38.651
So log of 3x,

01:42.272 --> 01:46.439
and since this function
right over here is defined

01:47.274 --> 01:50.089
and continuous over the
interval we care about,

01:50.089 --> 01:53.903
it's defined continuous for
all x's greater than zero,

01:53.903 --> 01:56.142
we can just substitute three in here

01:56.142 --> 01:58.016
to see what it would be approaching.

01:58.016 --> 02:02.183
So this would be equal to
log of three times three,

02:03.228 --> 02:06.759
or logarithm of nine, and once again

02:06.759 --> 02:09.240
when people just write log
here within writing the base,

02:09.240 --> 02:12.823
it's implied that it
is 10 right over here.

02:14.094 --> 02:15.963
So this is log base 10.

02:15.963 --> 02:17.853
That's just a good thing to know

02:17.853 --> 02:20.688
that sometimes gets missed a little bit.

02:20.688 --> 02:22.892
All right, now let's think
about the other case.

02:22.892 --> 02:25.218
Let's think about the
situation where we are

02:25.218 --> 02:27.440
approaching three from
the right hand side,

02:27.440 --> 02:29.764
from values greater than three.

02:29.764 --> 02:33.222
Well, we are now going
to be in this scenario

02:33.222 --> 02:36.576
right over there, so
this is going to be equal

02:36.576 --> 02:39.646
to the limit as x approaches three

02:39.646 --> 02:42.994
from the positive direction,
from the right hand side

02:42.994 --> 02:45.660
of, well g of x is in this clause

02:45.660 --> 02:47.854
when we are greater than three,

02:47.854 --> 02:50.937
so four minus x times log of nine,

02:53.013 --> 02:56.193
and this looks like some type
of a logarithm expression

02:56.193 --> 02:58.503
at first until you
realize that log of nine

02:58.503 --> 03:00.848
is just a constant, log base 10 of nine

03:00.848 --> 03:03.546
is gonna be some number close to one.

03:03.546 --> 03:06.710
This expression would
actually define a line.

03:06.710 --> 03:09.708
For x greater than or equal
to three, g of x is just

03:09.708 --> 03:12.175
a line even though it looks
a little bit complicated.

03:12.175 --> 03:16.030
And so this is actually
defined for all real numbers,

03:16.030 --> 03:20.197
and it's also continuous for
any x that you put into it.

03:21.600 --> 03:23.681
So to find this limit, to think about

03:23.681 --> 03:25.278
what is this expression approaching

03:25.278 --> 03:27.824
as we approach three from
the positive direction,

03:27.824 --> 03:29.950
well we can just evaluate a three.

03:29.950 --> 03:32.852
So it's going to be four minus three

03:32.852 --> 03:35.876
times log of nine, well that's just one,

03:35.876 --> 03:39.126
so that's equal to log base 10 of nine.

03:40.082 --> 03:44.091
So the limit from the left
equals the limit from the right.

03:44.091 --> 03:47.758
They're both log nine,
so the answer here is

03:49.454 --> 03:50.787
log log of nine,

03:53.746 --> 03:55.079
and we are done.
